<%!-- Hero Section --%>
<section class="relative bg-gradient-to-br from-pink-50 to-purple-50 pt-20">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900">
        Code of Conduct
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 mb-8">
        Our commitment to creating a safe, inclusive, and respectful environment for all members
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%!-- Decorative rainbow gradient --%>
  <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-400 via-yellow-400 via-green-400 via-blue-400 via-indigo-400 to-purple-400">
  </div>
</section>

<div class="min-h-screen bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <%!-- Introduction --%>
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-pink-50 to-purple-50 border-2 border-pink-200 rounded-lg p-8 mb-8">
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Ironfolk Combat strives to create an environment of safety, fun, and supportiveness that is accessible to anyone who wishes to participate. As a club, we organise around our core values which serve as a guide for members to ensure that we all participate in the way we mean to proceed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%!-- Core Values --%>
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center">
        <span class="w-2 h-8 bg-pink-500 mr-3 rounded"></span> Our Core Values
      </h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <%!-- Safety --%>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-pink-200 rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-pink-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3">
              <svg
                class="w-6 h-6 text-pink-600"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"
                >
                </path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Safety</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
            Safety is paramount. We recognize the inherent danger in our sport and take all necessary steps to ensure everyone's physical and emotional safety.
          </p>
        </div>

        <%!-- Camaraderie --%>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-purple-200 rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-purple-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3">
              <svg
                class="w-6 h-6 text-purple-600"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm6 3a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zM7 10a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0z"
                >
                </path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Camaraderie</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
            We build strong relationships and maintain an inclusive environment where all members feel recognized, valued, and heard.
          </p>
        </div>

        <%!-- Fun --%>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-pink-200 rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-pink-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3">
              <svg
                class="w-6 h-6 text-pink-600"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M14.828 14.828a4 4 0 01-5.656 0M9 10h.01M15 10h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"
                >
                </path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Fun</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
            Enjoying ourselves and the company we keep is a large part of why we do what we do. Fun is key to ensuring a successful and thriving club culture.
          </p>
        </div>

        <%!-- Learning --%>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-purple-200 rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center mb-4">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 bg-purple-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3">
              <svg
                class="w-6 h-6 text-purple-600"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              >
                <path
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="2"
                  d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.746 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.246 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253"
                >
                </path>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Learning</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
            We're a learning environment where all members can learn and teach. We're all here to be sword people, and learning is key to this goal.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%!-- Value Details --%>
    <div class="space-y-8 mb-12">
      <%!-- Safety Details --%>
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-pink-25 to-purple-25 border-l-4 border-pink-500 rounded-r-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Safety in Practice</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-pink-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We all take responsibility for ensuring safety during club activities</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-pink-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We wear correct protective equipment for our activity</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-pink-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We communicate clearly and seek consent</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-pink-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We recognize and understand the needs of others</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-pink-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We do not tolerate unsafe behaviour and speak up when necessary</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <%!-- Camaraderie Details --%>
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-25 to-pink-25 border-l-4 border-purple-500 rounded-r-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Building Community</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-purple-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We respect each other and listen actively</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-purple-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We include everyone and value their input</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 text-purple-600 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"
              >
              </path>
            </svg>
            <span>We seek to understand and resolve conflicts constructively</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%!-- Conduct Expectations --%>
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center">
        <span class="w-2 h-8 bg-purple-500 mr-3 rounded"></span> Conduct Expectations
      </h2>

      <%!-- Discrimination and Harassment --%>
      <div class="bg-white border-2 border-red-200 rounded-lg p-8 mb-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center">
          <svg
            class="w-6 h-6 text-red-600 mr-3"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          >
            <path
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              stroke-width="2"
              d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"
            >
            </path>
          </svg>
          Zero Tolerance: Discrimination and Harassment
        </h3>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-gray-700">
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">1. Celebrating Diversity</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              Ironfolk Combat celebrates diversity and recognizes value in growing more diverse. We will not tolerate discrimination for any reason. We aim to be a welcoming, safe space for diverse identities of culture, gender, sexuality, race, religion, politics, or otherwise.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">1a. Identity Validity</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              Any views that conflict with the validity of a member's identity are not welcome. This is not the place for discourse - it should be a given that members are entitled to their identity.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">2. Exclusionary Ideologies</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              We will not tolerate, welcome, or include any member with views that inherently disregard the validity of other cultures or identities including (but not limited to) Nazism, any form of White Supremacy, not recognizing gender diversity, or religion unable to tolerate diversity. If you're a Nazi, you aren't welcome in our club.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">3. Consent and Physical Boundaries</p>
            <p class="text-sm mb-2">
              There is no excuse for unwanted physical contact. We expect all members to ask for consent before touching another person and communicate clearly about physical boundaries.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              <strong>3a.</strong>
              Never assume consent unless an explicit discussion about implicit consent has occurred between members, and a distinct understanding has been reached.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">4. No Violence</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              While we practice controlled combat, violence of any kind will not be tolerated. Any action taken upon another member or property in anger or emotionally, with or without a weapon, will not be accepted.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">5. Anti-Bullying</p>
            <p class="text-sm">
              Bullying will not be tolerated. We take allegations seriously and expect members to receive feedback and change behavior. Failure to change will result in appropriate action.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%!-- Equipment/Property --%>
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 border-2 border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Equipment and Property</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 text-sm">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-blue-600 mr-2">•</span>
            <span>
              Treat all equipment (club and personal) with respect - as if it were your own, if not better
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-blue-600 mr-2">•</span>
            <span>Never intentionally damage equipment or property</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-blue-600 mr-2">•</span>
            <span>
              Ensure equipment is safe and maintained - remove burrs and sharp edges before use
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-blue-600 mr-2">•</span>
            <span>Wear adequate safety equipment as per Ironfolk guidelines</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <%!-- Event Conduct --%>
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-pink-50 border-2 border-purple-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Representing Ironfolk Combat</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
          Members are expected to comply with this Code of Conduct at any event, including those hosted by other clubs.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">
          Ironfolk Combat has established a reputation in the HEMA community for kinship and sportsmanship. Maintain positive, sporty conduct aligned with our values when representing the club.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm font-semibold">
          HEMA in Aotearoa New Zealand is a small community. We take our reputation seriously, and damage caused by individuals will be addressed appropriately.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%!-- Discipline --%>
    <div class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 flex items-center">
        <span class="w-2 h-8 bg-pink-500 mr-3 rounded"></span> Discipline and Enforcement
      </h2>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Members must comply with NZ law at all times while representing the club, and with local laws when visiting other countries as representatives. Illegal actions will be dealt with by appropriate authorities.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Breaches of the Code of Conduct will be handled case-by-case. We prefer a restorative, communication-based approach, but recognize this isn't always appropriate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <%!-- Major Misconduct --%>
        <div class="bg-red-50 border-2 border-red-300 rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-red-900 mb-4">Major Misconduct</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Intentional, recurring, repeated, or negative behavior breaching conduct expectations or values. May include illegal activity or actions impacting club reputation.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Possible Actions:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-700">
            <li>• Investigation</li>
            <li>• Immediate expulsion</li>
            <li>• Alerting authorities</li>
            <li>• Suspension from club/competition</li>
            <li>• Demotion from leadership</li>
            <li>• Other disciplinary action</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <%!-- Minor Misconduct --%>
        <div class="bg-yellow-50 border-2 border-yellow-300 rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-yellow-900 mb-4">Minor Misconduct</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Minor-scale breaches of club values or conduct expectations. Repeated breaches become Major Misconduct.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Restorative Approach:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-700">
            <li>• Behavioral discussion</li>
            <li>• Guidance on conduct</li>
            <li>• Mediation</li>
            <li>• Restorative processes</li>
            <li>• Formal warning</li>
            <li>• Temporary suspension</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%!-- Closing Note --%>
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-pink-50 to-purple-50 border-2 border-pink-200 rounded-lg p-8">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">A Note on Culture</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        A Code of Conduct might seem like a "doom and gloom" document for dealing with anti-social behavior. In practice, we aim for a culture where issues are legitimate mistakes or miscommunications, dealt with through immediate feedback and brave conversation.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        This document serves as a tool for situations where direct communication isn't possible or appropriate, and as a guide for achieving our desired culture together.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 font-semibold">
        By participating in club activities, members agree they have read, understood, and will act in accordance with club values and conduct expectations at all times.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
